theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("3_i6cpi")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 20
text = "God saw that the world had become full of wickedness and violence. People were doing evil, 
and this made God very disappointed. However, Noah was a righteous and obedient man,
so God chose him to survive a coming great flood.

God instructed Noah to build a huge ark (a large boat) to save his family and animals. 
He was told to bring his wife, his three sons (Shem, Ham, and Japheth), and their wives 
into the ark. God also commanded him to bring pairs of every kind of animal—male and female—so 
they could survive and repopulate the earth.

After Noah finished building the ark, rain fell for 40 days and 40 nights. The floodwaters covered 
the entire earth, destroying all living things outside the ark. Noah, his family, and the animals 
stayed safe inside.

After many months, the waters slowly went down. The ark finally came to rest on the mountains 
of Ararat. Noah sent out a raven and later a dove to check if the land was dry. When the dove 
returned with an olive leaf, Noah knew the flood was ending.

Once the land was dry, God told them to leave the ark. God then made a promise (covenant) never 
to destroy the earth with a flood again. As a sign of this promise, God placed a rainbow in the sky.

Mission find Noah and help him 

Tap screen to start"
horizontal_alignment = 1

